## Test-as-Contract Workflow

This project uses the `test-as-contract` workflow. Skills are installed under `.claude/skills/`.

### Available skills

| Skill | Purpose | Trigger |
|---|---|---|
| `/test-as-contract` | Start or continue a story | user |
| `/bootstrap-workflow` | Initialize project-level workflow infrastructure | user |
| `/demand-insight` | Adversarial demand interview | user |
| `/to-prd` | Synthesize discussion into PRD | user |
| `/design-system` | Build or verify project-level design system | user |
| `/ux-explore` | High-fidelity UX exploration with HTML prototypes | user |
| `/crystallize` | Convert PRD stable blocks into REQ-IDs | model |
| `/test-author` | Generate test scaffold from REQ | model |
| `/assertion-signoff` | Sign assertions before implementation | user |
| `/implementer` | Implement code against signed tests | model |
| `/qa-runner` | Run E2E, regression, collect evidence | model |
| `/feel-signoff` | Verify feel against HTML reference | user |
| `/reflect` | Capture lessons and update knowledge | user |

### Artifact layout

```
.aiassist/
├── stories/<story-id>/
│   ├── prd.md                 # Narrative intent (soft)
│   ├── requirements.md        # REQ with IDs (the contract)
│   ├── requirements-v1.hash   # Version hash for stale-test detection
│   ├── ux/                    # HTML UX references for feel-signoff
│   ├── test-plan.md           # Test-author's plan
│   ├── assertion-signoff.md       # Human assertion signoff
│   ├── feel-signoff.md        # Human feel verification
│   └── workflow-state.yaml    # Current phase / blockers
└── global/
    ├── engineering-lessons.md
    ├── architecture.md
    └── STANDARDS.md
```

### Core rules

1. **Truth flows down**: PRD → REQ → tests → code.
2. **Errors flow back up**: fix at the highest affected layer; never patch code directly because a test or spec is wrong.
3. **Assertions belong to the human**: AI writes test scaffolding; human signs expected values.
4. **Implementer is read-only on tests**: any diff touching test files invalidates the round.
5. **`/assertion-signoff` blocks BUILD; `/feel-signoff` blocks merge**.
6. **No test without a REQ-ID**: every test file must declare `// REQ-TRACE` and `// REQ-VERSION`.
7. **Subjective judgments stay out of tests**: feel/aesthetics are verified at feel-signoff against HTML references.

### Starting a new story

```
/test-as-contract
# or
/bootstrap-workflow
```

### Updating skills

When the canonical skills in `<workflow-path>/skills/` change, reinstall them:

```bash
rm -rf .claude/skills/*
cp -R <workflow-path>/skills/productivity/* .claude/skills/
cp -R <workflow-path>/skills/engineering/* .claude/skills/
```
